  "body": "## What happens\n\n- The Sodick Mark 21 post refuses each COMP record, so the control wire offset is not available.\n- The post accepts only G54 to G59.\n- The post writes no `M03` (AWT jump) before `T90`.\n\n## Expected\n\n- The Sodick Mark 21 programming manual gives `G40` / `G41` / `G42` with `H` registers. The post can use the shared helper `crates/post/src/post/wire_offset.rs`, as the LN2W post does (#4076).\n- The manual gives more work coordinate systems than G54-G59. The post can declare `workOffsetIndex` and map each index to its word.\n- The manual's AWT jump (`M03`) can be an option when `edm.awt` is true.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps:297-299`: each COMP record is refused (#1498).\n- `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps:337`: `/^G5[4-9]$/`.\n- `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps:44`, `:524`: `M03` is never written; `T90` stands alone.\n\nFound by the post audit against the Sodick manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\n- Each item is written or stays refused by name, with a golden and a decision entry.\n- Without these options, the Mark 21 output stays byte-identical.\n",
